# realtime — Ring-1 stratum: stream declarations (Riverwatch VII: Sparks move, Blocks remember)
stratum realtime "Stream semantics as data (round 5, answer #12: the terms the stranger correctly omitted and flagged). Sparks make no durability promise; Blocks make no latency promise; declaring both honestly is the point."

use units as units

term rate-hz : integer "Nominal message rate of a declared stream, in hertz."
term crystallize-every-s : integer "Checkpoint cadence: every N seconds the stream crystallizes a Block."

enum durability "What survives a sleep." { ephemeral checkpointed chained }

record stream-decl "A declared real-time stream on a publisher." {
    kind : text "The stream's kind name (e.g. hydro.stage-live)."
    rate : integer @unit = units:hertz "Nominal rate."
    survives : term-of durability "The durability promise, stated, not implied."
}
